details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two simple, matte ceramic plates positioned side by side, centered in the frame with generous negative space for a 3/4 overhead perspective at a 40-degree angle. Each plate contains a hearty serving of Southwestern tempeh scramble, featuring golden-browned crumbled tempeh mixed with sautéed bell peppers and translucent onions. The tempeh has a rustic, granular texture with deep amber hues from the cumin and smoked paprika. Halved cherry tomatoes with slightly softened, blistered skins are interspersed throughout. Diced, vibrant green avocado cubes and a generous scattering of fresh, bright green chopped cilantro are placed on top of the scramble. Beside each scramble on the same plate, two slightly charred whole-wheat tortillas are folded, showing natural creases. The surface is a rustic, aged oak wood table with visible grain and subtle wear. Props include a single wooden spoon resting casually on the wood surface near the plates and a small, slightly messy pile of loose cilantro leaves and a stray diced avocado piece near the edge. The lighting is soft, natural side light from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the oily sheen on the tempeh. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a tiny sauce drip on the plate rim, slightly uneven browning on the tempeh. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few stray crumbs on the wooden surface. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
  }
]
